I have a benchmark that spawns a goroutine inside the loop to do async work:

```go
func BenchmarkProcess(b *testing.B) {
    b.ReportAllocs()
    for b.Loop() {
        ch := make(chan Result, 1)
        go worker(ch)  // worker allocates internally
        <-ch
    }
}
```

The benchmark reports 1 alloc/op (just the channel). But profiling shows the worker goroutine allocates heavily. Why doesn't ReportAllocs see those?
